// repro-25 — E-CODEGEN-INVALID-JS: binding an SSE generator inside `on mount {}`
// emits unparseable JS.
//
// Compiler: ../scrml @ ca712295 (s212). Command: scrml compile repro-25-...scrml
// Expected: compiles (an SSE binding in on-mount is the natural "start the stream
//   after first render" lifecycle). Actual: a "statement boundary not detected"
//   warning + E-CODEGEN-INVALID-JS (the compiler emits JS it cannot itself parse).
//
// Workaround (what giti's feed.scrml uses): bind at module top in a ${} logic
// block instead — `${ @status = tick() }` compiles cleanly. Only the on-mount
// placement trips the codegen.

<program>

${
  server function* tick() {
    while (true) {
      yield { event: "t", data: { n: 1 } }
    }
  }
}

<status> = { n: 0 }
on mount { @status = tick() }

<p>${@status.n}</p>

</program>
